[0m[38;2;255;255;255m● [0m1. Bananas are berries, botanically speaking.
  2. Strawberries are not true berries, and each "seed" on them is a tiny fruit of its own.
  3. Tomatoes are fruits, botanically speaking. 
  4. Apples float because about a quarter of their volume is air. 
  5. Pineapple contains bromelain, an enzyme that breaks down protein.
  6. An avocado is a berry with a single seed.
  7. A raspberry is an aggregate fruit made of many small drupelets.
  8. Ripe cranberries bounce, and growers have used that to sort them.
  9. Kiwifruit used to be sold as the "Chinese gooseberry."
  10. Grapefruit can change how the body breaks down some medications.
  11. Peaches and nectarines are the same species, and nectarines are smooth because of one recessive gene.
  12. Each cashew nut grows attached to a fleshy fruit called the cashew apple.
  13. Durian is banned on Singapore's public transit because of its smell.
  14. Over 7,500 varieties of apple are grown around the world.
  15. A single pomegranate can hold hundreds of juicy seeds, called arils.
  16. A fig is really a cluster of flowers turned inward.
  17. Watermelon is about 92% water.
  18. Blueberries get their color from pigments called anthocyanins.
  19. A coconut is a drupe, not a true nut.
  20. Mangoes are related to cashews and pistachios.
  21. Bananas are slightly radioactive because of the potassium-40 they contain.
  22. Apples, pears, cherries and plums all belong to the rose family.
  23. The sweet orange is thought to be a hybrid of pomelo and mandarin.
  24. The Cavendish is the banana most of the world exports.
  25. Grapes and raisins can cause kidney failure in dogs.
  26. A pineapple plant takes well over a year to produce one fruit.
  27. Dragon fruit grows on a climbing cactus.
  28. A jackfruit can weigh more than 30 kg, making it the largest fruit that grows on trees.
  29. Miracle fruit contains miraculin, a protein that makes sour foods taste sweet.
  30. Cherry pits contain amygdalin, which can release cyanide when crushed.
  31. Ripening apples give off ethylene, a gas that speeds up the ripening of fruit nearby.
  32. Bell peppers are fruits, botanically speaking.
  33. By weight, a kiwifruit has more vitamin C than an orange.
  34. Plantains are bananas that are usually cooked before eating.
  35. Olives are drupes, the same type of fruit as cherries.
  36. A US court ruled in 1947 that rhubarb counts as a fruit for customs, although it is a vegetable botanically.
  37. The part of a lychee you eat is a fleshy layer around the seed called an aril.
  38. Astringent persimmons are full of tannins until they are completely ripe.
  39. Seedless watermelons are triploid, so they can't produce mature seeds.
  40. Raw quinces are hard and sour, so they are almost always cooked.
  
  The plant world sorts fruit quite differently from the kitchen.

